# gobot repo line-ending policy.
#
# The repo stores text files with LF. Without an explicit policy git is forced
# to guess on Windows checkouts (where autocrlf=true is the default), producing
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" warnings on every
# edit and letting CRLF leak into tracked files.
#
# eol=lf means: store LF in the repo, check out LF in the working tree.
#
# Unlike the Crucible repo, adopting this file DID require a renormalization
# pass: 20 tracked files held CRLF or mixed endings when it was added. The
# .crucible/ subtree keeps its own .gitattributes and is unaffected.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.go    text eol=lf
*.mod   text eol=lf
*.sum   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
